WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.234
-Enjoy yourself.
Welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:04.567
to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:05.567
You're here.
You made it.

00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:07.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:09.467
I'm so excited about this.

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:12.367
Today is our ninth anniversary
on "The Tonight Show."

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:15.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:17.834
♪♪

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:19.367
That's right.

00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:23.434
Nine years, 1,800 episodes, and
one really awkward conversation

00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:24.434
with Nicole Kidman.

00:00:24.434 --> 00:00:27.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:29.934
Yep, nine years.

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:32.400
Of course, we've had some work
done, so we only look seven.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.534
Nine years, that means the show
is officially halfway

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:38.067
to dating Leonardo DiCaprio.

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:39.501
[ Audience gasps ]

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:40.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:43.334
-Oh, no, you didn't.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:44.968
Oh, come on.

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:46.467
-Our show --
-Come on.

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:50.767
-Our show premiered
during the 2014 Winter Olympics.

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:52.334
That's how long it's been.

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:54.133
We started way back
when there was still winter.

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:57.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:59.567
It's a major accomplishment,
and as a thank you

00:00:59.567 --> 00:01:02.501
to the entire staff, I gave them
off for Presidents' Day weekend.

00:01:02.501 --> 00:01:04.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:07.968
The traditional gift for the
ninth anniversary is pottery,

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:10.000
so, later tonight, Tariq
and I will be re-enacting

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.300
the scene from "Ghost."

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:20.033
That's right. We've been on
the air for a whole nine years.

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:21.734
I can't believe it.
A lot has changed since then.

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:24.834
I mean, look, this is a picture
of me when I first started.

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:26.167
That's real. Yeah.

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:27.167
[ Audience awws ]

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:28.968
Here's a picture of you, Tariq.

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:31.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.167
Can you believe
that was nine years ago?

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:34.167
And here's a picture of you,
Higgins.

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:35.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:36.801
-Aww.
-That's not --

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:40.067
-A long time ago.
-Nine years ago. Yeah, nine.

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:41.400
Time flies.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.400
Well, as I mentioned,
it's Presidents' Day weekend.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.834
Of course, every family
is different.

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:46.334
Some families get together
on Presidents' Day,

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:48.834
while others celebrate
on Presidents' Day eve.

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:50.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.734 --> 00:01:52.133
Yep, not only is there
a long weekend,

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:53.501
but everyone's pumped
for this --

00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:56.501
today "Ant-Man And The Wasp:
Quantumania" hit theaters.

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:58.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:00.367
Yeah.

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:03.334
Which is great because usually
to see ants at a theater,

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:04.534
you have to go to
go to Regal Cinemas.

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:06.234
[ Audience ohs ]

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:08.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:09.167
[ Mimics cigarette drag ]
"Sit whatever you want.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:10.234
I don't care where."

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:11.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:12.300
"My seat doesn't go back."

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.400
"Well, I know,
but it goes forward."

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.901
Why would I --

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:19.868
Meanwhile, I heard that in
the future, Disney wants

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:22.400
to spread out
their Marvel releases. Yeah.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.701
Disney knew it was time to slow
down when they started making

00:02:24.701 --> 00:02:26.334
a movie about The Hulk's tailor.

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:29.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.801
"I work on his suits
all the time.

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:35.133
I say please don't get angry,
Mr. Banner.

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:36.701
You'll ruin..."

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:38.033
Some news from Washington --

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:40.501
President Biden just had
his annual physical exam,

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:43.767
and his doctor reported that
Biden is "healthy and vigorous."

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:46.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.100
Even Democrats are like,
"Healthy and vigorous?

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.434
Did he go to Trump's doctor?

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:56.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:58.767
When Biden left the room,
the doctor was like, "Yeesh!"

00:02:58.767 --> 00:03:00.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:03.567
Yep, Biden's doctor said
he's healthy and vigorous,

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:06.200
but has a stiff gait.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.367
He basically got the same
results as Seabiscuit.

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:10.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:13.400
Biden's doctor also said
he had a small lesion removed

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:16.000
